Leasehold improvements are amortized on a straight-line basis over the shorter of their estimated useful lives or the term of the lease. Depreciation expense was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_uvc8ZF6Js0-z81tYLF8nVg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_tofE_XZPmUi1m7ytubGWZQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" id="Narr_SDQlNqNF6Eej-6bEOUxuhw">0.4</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_uvc8ZF6Js0-z81tYLF8nVg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_mJsINAvwa0mYh9rNp_Cl1Q" decimals="-5" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" name="us-gaap:Depreciation" scale="6" id="Narr_Ouk3QP9wWUKFhJG3_sv2Vg">0.2</ix:nonFraction> million for the&#160;years ended December 31, 2022 and 2021, respectively. </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Arial','Helvetica','sans-serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:12pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">88</p></div></div>
